Codes. There are significant public and first responder safety concerns with Single Exit Stairways (SES). | Ensuring Firefighters Are Protected from PFAS (Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances); Endorsement of UBCM 2024 Resolution NR37 Provincial Funding for PFAS-Free Firefighting Gear; 
Provide provincial subsidy funding specifically for the procurement of PFAS-free bunker gear for all BC firefighters, to prioritize their health and safety while ensuring their gear meets the highest standards of protection and safety without the use of PFAS and exposure to the harmful effects of these forever chemicals, and work towards the introduction of alternatives to PFAS-containing fire retardant foam. | Ensuring Firefighters Are Protected from PFAS (Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances); Endorsement of UBCM 2024 Resolution NR37: Provide provincial subsidy funding specifically for the procurement of PFAS-free bunker gear for all BC firefighters, to prioritize their health and safety while ensuring their gear meets the highest standards of protection and safety without the use of PFAS and exposure to the harmful effects of these forever chemicals, and work towards the introduction of alternatives to PFAS-containing fire retardant foam. | Endorsement of BluePrint's Proposal Resilience Program Funding for Fire Fighters and Police Officers. | Discussion regarding proposed amendments to the BC Building Code regarding single egress stairways for taller residential buildings. | Discussion and exploring ways to improve recruitment, education and awareness of fire service; job requirements; certifications; | Advocacy regarding changes to emergency medical responses in relation to the General Auditors report of 2019 that calls for greater collaboration and coordination of emergency services.) BC Ministries/Provincial Entities: Finance, Labour, Office of the Premier, Public Safety and Solicitor General, WorkSafeBC, Health, Member(s) of the BC Legislative Assembly, Forests, Post-Secondary Education and Future Skills, Housing and Municipal Affairs, Minister of State for Community Safety and Integrated Services Lobbyists Details Lobbyists Employed: Brian Catinus, Todd Schierling

