ds announcement and the future engagement and partnership the Province seeks to have with private sector home builders. | BC Build program and initiatives to standardized applications and streamline approvals for multiplex projects. | As part of CHBA BC's Day at the Legislature event, discussed priorities and further action that can be taken around streamline housing approvals, low carbon solutions, and reducing the costs of new homes. This included further improvements to provincial regulations, expanded funded for CleanBC incentives to energy retrofits, and reforms to development finance tools. Initiatives underway to address workforce labour challenges were also discussed. | Addressing the costs to build homes specifically through improvement of development finance tools such as DCCs, CACs, PST and more.) BC Ministries/Provincial Entities: Finance, Labour, Office of the Premier, Member(s) of the BC Legislative Assembly, Parliamentary Secretary for Rural Development, Attorney General, Emergency Management and Climate Readiness, Forests, Post-Secondary Education and Future Skills, Water, Land and Resource Stewardship, Housing and Municipal Affairs, Jobs and Economic Growth Lobbyists Details Lobbyists Employed: Heesoo Scott, Pauline Rupp, Neil Moody

